# {{Service}} — observability catalog

Assets in this folder travel with the service when it is extracted (rule O-8).

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `slo.yaml` | SLIs/SLOs; `tools/gen_slo_rules.py` turns it into burn-rate alert rules |
| `alerts.rules.yaml` | Hand-written cause alerts (generated SLO rules are emitted separately) |
| `dashboards/` | Grafana dashboards (JSON), provisioned as code |
| `runbook.md` | One section per alert; every alert's `runbook_url` points here |

## Metrics (business)
| Name | Type | Attributes (closed sets) | Meaning |
|---|---|---|---|
| `{{service}}.ping.received` | counter | `outcome` ∈ {ok} | SAMPLE — replace |

RED metrics (`http.server.request.duration`, …) are automatic and carry `app.service={{service}}`.

## Log events (constant `event` names)
`ping_handled`, plus `http_request_completed` / `request_failed` from the platform.

## Spans
`{{service}}.Ping` (use case), `{{service}}_contracts.{{Service}}Api.ping` (contract call), `events.publish {{service}}.ping_received.v1`.
